==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Wargod Nobunaga''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Immortal Nobunaga''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

Evolves into '''Phantasmal Nobunaga''' at level 60 using [[Catfruit]], [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Oda Nobunaga can essentially perma-freeze Dark enemies from a great distance, and his uptime can completely stop them from pushing as long as he lands his first hit on them, all while doing decent damage. While Dark enemies are usually knocked back easily, he does enough damage to stagger them, and those that have few knockbacks like [[Le'noir|Le'Noir]] are rendered helpless because they cannot reposition to break free. The few Darks that cause trouble for him, such as [[Ragin' Gory]] and [[Director Kurosawah|Kurosawah]], aren't that problematic either, as accessible counters exist for them.

However, this unit sees serious competition from various other anti-Dark specialists. For freezing Dark enemies, [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] can do the job, and while it's [[Bloomin' Brightly (Easy)|difficult to obtain]] with lower range, its much faster cooldown allows it to be simply replaced whenever if it fails. Most ranged Darks have a slow attack rate, so Bomber is already sufficient with stopping the pushers. In comparison, Oda Nobunaga's cooldown, while shorter than the average Uber, is still way too long and his singular knockback further reduces his survivability, even if it means allowing him to tank and get a freeze in. Oda is not the most efficient at killing such enemies either due to the existence of [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza]], as well as the fact that his damage is only average, even with his specialist performance factored in.

==='''True Form'''===
Immortal Nobunaga gets more health and damage, which do improve his stats for general use and allows him to survive a bit longer when under fire from enemy surges, waves and Long Distance attacks. His freeze duration also improves, but due to it having full uptime already, it doesn't necessarily make him better. In fact, if anything, his attacks can potentially cause Darks to stay frozen while out of range, forcing your units to move up instead of being able to comfortably lure them and exploit their range disadvantage.

==='''Ultra Form'''===
This form is prohibitively expensive for many due to the large cost of Dark Catseyes and Behemoth Gems. However, Phantasmal Nobunaga receives multiple notable buffs in exchange.

The first is the ability to freeze [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku enemies]]. Due to his high range and 100% freeze chance, he does it surprisingly well as long as he gets a shot on, and his range keeps him safe. However, while he still has the permafreeze potential that he does against Dark enemies, his foreswing, cost, and cooldown can still make him awkward to use. Additionally, he lacks the ability to deal with enemy Shields. Just as many Dark enemies can reposition to break free, Aku enemies can reposition on health loss, subsequently regenerating their Shields as well for them to eventually break free (if they have one), so support is still needed to get past them and ensure he hits. Still, he functions quite well against [[Aku Gory]], [[Condemned Peng]] and many others that do not have Shields, since he can consistently outrange them and ensure they'll never get to push.

The second is improved survivability. His HP is increased by over 44%, reaching 176,000 at level 60 without accounting for talents. This is far from ideal for tanking, but the extra survivability does make it easier for him to get started. Additionally, he gains a second knockback, which allows him to reposition safely from a high-DPS horde. Dark and Aku enemies can both be brutal with DPS, so tanking is often impractical with a need to reposition. Finally, while he is not immune to the [[Surge Attack]]s that many Aku attackers are known to launch, he can duplicate Surges, allowing him to freeze threats that are much further away from him. However, while they do benefit him in some way, it is still generally impractical as tanking Surges repeatedly without defensive abilities to cut their damage can and will result in them quickly tearing down his health before he can be replaced.

Overall, while Oda Nobunaga does improve a lot with this form, it may not be worth the exorbitant cost.

==='''Talents'''===
Curse Immunity is not very useful for this unit. He does not target Relics, and while this can see use when Darks are supported by enemies that employ Curse like Loris in [[Miracle Iris (Deadly)|Miracle Iris]] and [[Relic Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Relic Doge Base]] in [[Cats in the Stars]], it remains situational for its cost. The same can be said for Wave Resist, Attack Buff and HP Buff, as Oda is not particularly useful for tanking or dealing damage in general, and therefore not worth investing lots of NP for a small boost. Move Speed Up is usually detrimental, since while Oda is slow, all aggressive Dark pushers are already pretty fast, meaning extra speed isn't needed for him to engage them at all. Survive is perhaps the best talent since Oda's high range allows him to continue supporting your units for a fair while, but it still isn't too special.

==='''Orb'''===
Defense Orb for better tanking, or Surge Resist Ability Orb for survivability against Surge Attacks and improved Counter-Surge activation.

